{#
Le générateur de cartes Open Graph : une page de 1200 × 630 pixels, en haut
à gauche, qui affiche le site suivi de votre choix.

La page suit le même modèle que celle des cartes d’11ty-website : une page
dont les dimensions correspondent exactement à celles de l’image, capturée
par un service plutôt que composée pendant la génération du site, avec
l’interface d’édition placée sous la zone visible. Le paramètre
`?site=<slug>` permet de choisir le site et fournit à chaque carte une URL
	stable. La liste déroulante permet de trouver son identifiant.

	Tout le contenu de la carte est calculé ici et transmis sous forme de
	données : le script ci-dessous ne tire aucune conclusion, il insère
	uniquement des valeurs dans une structure déjà créée. Les couleurs des
	anneaux proviennent notamment de `lib/rank.js`, utilisé aussi par les
	anneaux des pages du site, via les filtres `scoreClass`, `axeClass` et
	`cwvClass`. La couleur d’un cercle sur la carte correspond donc toujours
	à celle de la page représentée.
	-#}
	<!doctype html>
	<html lang="fr">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8">
		<title>Générateur de cartes Open Graph · {{ meta.title }}</title>
		<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
		{#- La feuille de style est liée plutôt qu’intégrée directement : la carte
		réutilise les variables CSS du site, les règles des anneaux et celles des
		icônes des outils. Il n’est pas nécessaire de les dupliquer. -#}
		<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
<style>
/* Dark unconditionally. A card is one image on somebody else's timeline, so it
   cannot follow a reader's preference the way the site does. */
/* Everything outside the 1200×630 frame is painted darker than the card, so the
   capture area is visible as a rectangle while you work. Nothing of this reaches
   the image — the card covers the whole capture — it exists to show you where
   the edge is. The card itself keeps --bg, which is the site's own page color.

   On both html and body, and body is the one that matters: style.css already
   sets `body { background: var(--bg) }`, which paints the full content box and
   would otherwise cover an html background entirely. */
html,
body {
	background: #141414;
}
html {
	/* A scrollbar would eat 15px off the right edge of a 1200px capture. */
	scrollbar-width: none;
}
html::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
body { margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* The capture target, at the top left of the viewport so a 1200×630 screenshot
   takes it edge to edge. */
.og {
	box-sizing: border-box;
	width: 1200px;
	height: 630px;
	padding: 42px 64px;
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	justify-content: space-between;
	gap: 20px;
	overflow: hidden;
	background: var(--bg);
	color: var(--text);
	font-family: var(--sans);
	-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}
.og > * { flex: none; }
.og p { margin: 0; }

.og-top {
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	gap: 14px;
	font-size: 30px;
	font-weight: 650;
}
.og-mark { width: 34px; height: 34px; color: var(--brand); }
.og-eyebrow {
	margin-left: auto;
	font-size: 24px;
	font-weight: 600;
	color: var(--text-muted-strong);
	padding: 0.35em 0.9em;
	border: 2px solid var(--border-strong);
	border-radius: var(--pill);
	white-space: nowrap;
	overflow: hidden;
	max-width: 42%;
	text-overflow: ellipsis;
}
.og-eyebrow:empty { display: none; }

/* Two classes, to outweigh the `.og p` margin reset above — this is a <p>. */
.og .og-name {
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	gap: 20px;
	font-size: 76px; /* resized to fit by the script */
	font-weight: 700;
	/* Enough for descenders: the line box is also the clipping box here, and at
	   1.05 a `g` or `y` in a domain lost its tail. */
	line-height: 1.25;
	letter-spacing: -0.02em;
	overflow: hidden;
	white-space: nowrap;
	margin-bottom: 18px;
}
.og-name img {
	flex: none;
	width: 1em;
	height: 1em;
	border-radius: 6px;
}
.og-name img:not([src]) { display: none; }
/* Spacing lives on .og-name above: these are adjacent block boxes, so a margin
   here would collapse with that one rather than add to it. */
.og-meta {
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	gap: 12px;
	font-size: 24px;
	color: var(--text-muted-strong);
}
.og-rank {
	font-weight: 650;
	color: var(--text);
	border: 2px solid var(--border-strong);
	border-radius: var(--pill);
	padding: 0.2em 0.7em;
}
.og-stack {
	display: inline-flex;
	align-items: center;
	gap: 10px;
	color: var(--text);
	font-weight: 600;
}
/* The separator is a flex child of the item it precedes, so the row's own gap
   sits before it and this one after. Never on the first item, which happens on
   a site with no rank line to follow. */
.og-stack:not(:first-child)::before {
	content: "\00b7";
	color: var(--text-muted);
}
/* The letter-pair fallback for a brand with no mark is sized for a table row. */
.og-stack .stack-chip {
	font-size: 15px;
	line-height: 30px;
	min-width: 30px;
}

/* Width and height rather than a bigger `size` argument, so the stroke and the
   text scale with the box — the same trick .detail-rings uses. */
.og-rings { display: flex; gap: 22px; }
/* An author `display` beats the UA stylesheet's `[hidden]`, as with the figure
   row below. */
.og-rings[hidden] { display: none; }
/* Fixed to the ring's own width, so a long label wraps inside its column
   instead of widening it — six labels of six different lengths otherwise space
   the row six different ways. */
.og-ring {
	width: 116px;
	text-align: center;
}
.og-ring .ring { width: 116px; height: 116px; }
.og-ring-label {
	display: block;
	margin-top: 10px;
	font-size: 14px;
	font-weight: 600;
	line-height: 1.25;
	letter-spacing: 0.02em;
	text-transform: uppercase;
	color: var(--text-muted-strong);
}

.og-bottom {
	display: flex;
	align-items: flex-end;
	justify-content: space-between;
	gap: 32px;
	padding-top: 26px;
	border-top: 3px solid var(--border);
}
.og-figures { display: flex; gap: 44px; }
/* An author `display` beats the UA stylesheet's `[hidden] { display: none }`,
   so hiding this row needs saying explicitly. */
.og-figures[hidden] { display: none; }
.og-figure[hidden] { display: none; }
.og-figure-label {
	display: block;
	font-size: 17px;
	font-weight: 600;
	letter-spacing: 0.04em;
	text-transform: uppercase;
	color: var(--text-muted);
}
.og-figure-value {
	display: block;
	margin-top: 4px;
	font-size: 34px;
	font-weight: 650;
	font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
}
/* The last runs as two rows of six dots — the same mark the Recently measured
   list uses, scaled up from its 5px table size. */
.og-runs {
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	gap: 6px;
	margin-top: 6px;
}
.og-runs .recents-dots { gap: 5px; }
.og-runs .recents-dot { width: 12px; height: 12px; }

.og-empty {
	display: inline-flex;
	align-items: center;
	gap: 6px;
	margin-left: 8px;
	font-size: 17px;
	font-weight: 700;
	letter-spacing: 0.04em;
	text-transform: uppercase;
	color: var(--poor-text);
	vertical-align: 0.15em;
}
.og-date { font-size: 22px; color: var(--text-muted); white-space: nowrap; }
/* The unmeasured state takes the figures' place rather than sitting beside
   them, so the rule above it still spans the card. */
.og-unmeasured { font-size: 34px; color: var(--text-muted-strong); }

/* Editor UI, below the fold so it stays out of every capture. */
.ui {
	max-width: 1200px;
	padding: 44px 64px 90px;
	font-size: 16px;
	line-height: 1.5;
	color: var(--text-muted-strong);
	font-family: var(--sans);
}
.ui h2 { font-size: 18px; margin: 0 0 0.4em; color: var(--text); }
.ui p { margin: 0 0 1.2em; }
.ui-fields {
	display: grid;
	grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(17rem, 1fr));
	gap: 1rem;
	max-width: 44rem;
	margin-bottom: 1.2em;
}
.ui label { display: grid; gap: 0.4em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); min-width: 0; }
/* The select takes the room, the count sits beside it and never wraps. */
.ui-field-row {
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	gap: 0.6em;
	min-width: 0;
}
.ui-field-row select { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
.ui-count { font-weight: 500; color: var(--text-muted); white-space: nowrap; }
.ui select {
	font: inherit;
	padding: 0.5em 0.6em;
	border: 2px solid var(--border-strong);
	border-radius: 6px;
	background: var(--surface);
	color: var(--text);
}
.ui code { font-family: var(--mono); word-break: break-all; color: var(--text); }
.ui-problem {
	font-family: var(--mono);
	font-size: 14px;
	white-space: pre-wrap;
	padding: 1em 1.2em;
	border: 2px solid var(--poor);
	border-radius: 6px;
	color: var(--poor-text);
	background: var(--poor-bg);
}
.ui-problem[hidden] { display: none; }
.ui-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; align-items: center; margin: 20px 0 24px; }
.ui-actions a[hidden] { display: none; }
.ui button,
.ui-actions a {
	font: inherit;
	font-weight: 600;
	cursor: pointer;
	padding: 0.55em 1.2em;
	border: 2px solid var(--border-strong);
	border-radius: var(--pill);
	background: var(--button);
	color: var(--text);
	text-decoration: none;
	line-height: 1;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="og" id="og">
	<div class="og-top">
		<i class="fa-solid fa-forward-fast og-mark" width="34" height="34" aria-hidden="true"></i>
		{{ meta.title }}
		<span class="og-eyebrow" id="og-eyebrow"></span>
	</div>

	<div>
		<p class="og-name" id="og-name">
			<img id="og-favicon" width="64" height="64" alt="" decoding="async">
			<span id="og-domain">{{ meta.url | hostname }}</span>
		</p>
		<p class="og-meta" id="og-meta"></p>
	</div>

	{#
	Les anneaux sont affichés ici à l’aide des mêmes shortcodes que ceux
	utilisés sur les pages du site, avec des valeurs provisoires. Le script
	ne modifie que les éléments variables : la classe de bande, le tiret de
	l’arc et le texte au centre. La géométrie des anneaux n’est donc pas
	reproduite dans le navigateur : la circonférence est lue directement
	sur l’arc déjà dessiné.

	Les valeurs provisoires sont utilisées plutôt que les résultats d’un
	vrai site, car chacune doit produire un arc : le shortcode omet entièrement
	l’arc si la valeur est null, et le script ne peut pas remplir un élément
	qui n’a jamais été affiché.
	#}
	<div class="og-rings" id="og-rings" hidden>
		{% for score in metrics.SCORES %}
		<span class="og-ring">
			{% scoreRing 100, score.label, score.short %}
			<span class="og-ring-label">{{ score.label }}</span>
		</span>
		{% endfor %}
		<span class="og-ring">
			{% axeRing 0 %}
			<span class="og-ring-label">Axe</span>
		</span>
		<span class="og-ring">
			{% cwvRing 0, 3 %}
			<span class="og-ring-label">Core Web Vitals</span>
		</span>
	</div>

	<div class="og-bottom">
		<div class="og-figures" id="og-figures">
			<span class="og-figure" id="og-fig-weight">
				<span class="og-figure-label">Poids de la page</span>
				<span class="og-figure-value"></span>
			</span>
			<span class="og-figure" id="og-fig-requests">
				<span class="og-figure-label">Requêtes</span>
				<span class="og-figure-value"></span>
			</span>
			<span class="og-figure" id="og-fig-lcp">
				<span class="og-figure-label">LCP</span>
				<span class="og-figure-value"></span>
			</span>
			{#- Affiché uniquement lorsqu’une capture sans JavaScript a été enregistrée. Même condition que pour la section correspondante de la page du site. -#}
			<span class="og-figure" id="og-fig-nojs" hidden>
				<span class="og-figure-label">Sans JS &#8710;</span>
				<span class="og-figure-value"></span>
			</span>
			{#- Les deux mesures les plus récentes, dans l’ordre chronologique, sous forme des six bandes de chacune. Il s’agit d’une représentation visuelle, pas d’une valeur : elle permet de voir si la dernière mesure ressemble à la précédente. -#}
			<span class="og-figure" id="og-fig-runs" hidden>
				<span class="og-figure-label"></span>
				<span class="og-runs"></span>
			</span>
		</div>
		<p class="og-unmeasured" id="og-unmeasured" hidden">Pas encore mesuré.</p>
		<p class="og-date" id="og-date"></p>
	</div>
</div>

<div class="ui">
	<h2>Carte Open Graph</h2>
	<p>La carte ci-dessus mesure exactement 1200&times;630 pixels et se trouve en haut à gauche de cette page. Tout ce qui se trouve en dessous, ainsi que la zone plus sombre qui l’entoure, n’apparaît pas dans la capture.</p>

	{#- Deux étapes plutôt qu’une liste déroulante de 1 500 éléments. La catégorie réduit la liste ; seul le site détermine l’URL, et la catégorie est ensuite récupérée depuis celle-ci. -#}
	<div class="ui-fields">
		<label>Catégorie
			<select id="field-category"></select>
		</label>
		<label>Site
			<span class="ui-field-row">
				<select id="field-site"></select>
				<span class="ui-count" id="ui-site-count"></span>
			</span>
		</label>
	</div>

	<div class="ui-actions">
		<button type="button" id="copy-link">Copier le lien de cette carte</button>
		<a id="open-screenshot" href="" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ouvrir l’URL de la capture</a>
		<a id="open-report" href="">Rapport complet</a>
		<a id="open-category" href="">Catégorie</a>
	</div>

	<p>Image générée à partir de : <code id="ui-screenshot-url"></code></p>

	{#- Même si la carte ne s’affiche pas correctement, elle doit conserver son apparence. Le squelette ci-dessous, visible avant l’exécution du script, est crédible : il affiche des centaines partout et le domaine du site. En cas d’erreur, le message s’affiche donc ici plutôt que seulement dans la console, où personne ne penserait à regarder après avoir vu une image incorrecte. -#}
	<p id="ui-problem" class="ui-problem" hidden></p>
</div>

{#
Une icône par générateur ou hébergeur distinct, affichée une seule fois et
dupliquée par le script. Les icônes ne figurent pas dans le JSON ci-dessous :
`stackIcon` génère un élément Font Awesome `<i>` pour les marques prises en
	charge par Font Awesome, qui ne devient un glyphe que lorsque le plugin
	transforme du véritable code HTML. Un élément inclus dans une chaîne JSON
	n’est jamais détecté. Le clonage permet aussi de n’avoir qu’une seule copie
	du chemin d’une icône de marque utilisée par 700 sites.

	Les éléments sont indexés par leur nom, comme dans le récapitulatif des
	outils. Ainsi, une catégorie regroupée comme « Hébergé soi-même » utilise
	sa propre icône plutôt que celle du logiciel qui se trouve derrière, laquelle
	est affichée sur les pages des sites.
	#}
	<div id="og-marks" hidden>
		<span data-icon="warning">{#- Cloné dans la valeur « Sans JS ». -#}<i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
		{%- for item in sites.stacks.generators.items %}<span data-mark="{{ item.name }}">{% stackIcon item, 30 %}</span>{% endfor -%}
		{%- for item in sites.stacks.hosts.items %}<span data-mark="{{ item.name }}">{% stackIcon item, 30 %}</span>{% endfor -%}
	</div>

	{#
	Tous les sites suivis, sous forme de tableaux plutôt que d’objets : il y a
	environ 1 500 enregistrements, et les clés représenteraient une grande
	partie du poids total. La légende se trouve dans le script ci-dessous.

	Le 0 initial simplifie la gestion des virgules dans la boucle. Il est retiré
	de l’autre côté, selon la même astuce que sur la page des cartes du site
	11ty-website.
	#}
	{#
	Les catégories sont présentées dans le même ordre que sur le site : d’abord
	celles affichées sur la page d’accueil, dans l’ordre de `sites.groups`, puis
	les autres. La page de sélection des catégories dans base.njk procède de la
	même manière, pour la même raison : une catégorie absente de la page d’accueil
	reste accessible, mais apparaît après celles auxquelles les lecteurs
	s’attendent. Un tri alphabétique dans le navigateur aurait donné à cette liste
	un ordre différent de celui utilisé ailleurs sur le site.

	Chaque élément est une paire `[nom, identifiant]` : les enregistrements
	contiennent le nom de la catégorie, et sa page est désignée par son
	identifiant.
	#}
	<script type="application/json" id="og-categories">
[0
{%- for g in sites.groups %}{% if g.showOnHomePageCategoryList %},{{ [g.name, g.id] | dump | replace("</", "<\\/") | safe }}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- for g in sites.groups %}{% if not g.showOnHomePageCategoryList %},{{ [g.name, g.id] | dump | replace("</", "<\\/") | safe }}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
]
	</script>

	<script type="application/json" id="og-sites">
		[0
			{%- for entry in sites.entries -%}
			{%- set lab = entry.latest.lab if entry.latest -%}
			{%- set rings = [] -%}
			{%- for score in metrics.SCORES -%}
			{%- set v = lab.scores[score.key] if lab else null -%}
			{%- set rings = (rings.push([v | scoreClass, v]), rings) -%}
			{%- endfor -%}
			{#- Reproduit le comportement de axeRing : un test ayant échoué ne fournit aucun décompte, et l’absence de décompte correspond à « aucun ». -#}
			{%- set axeValue = entry.axe.violations if entry.axe and not entry.axe.error else null -%}
			{%- set rings = (rings.push([axeValue | axeClass, null]), rings) -%}
			{%- set rings = (rings.push([entry.cwvFailures | cwvClass(entry.cwvWorst or "poor"), null]), rings) -%}
			{#- Un classement ne mérite d’apparaître sur une carte que s’il est flatteur ; les anneaux affichés à côté permettent de le déterminer. « N° 812 » au-dessus d’un cercle orange serait contradictoire. Seuls le vert et le gris sont acceptés : un test axe non effectué et un site jamais échantillonné par CrUX sont des absences de données, pas des points négatifs.

				On examine les six bandes affichées sur la carte plutôt que `allGreen`, qui ne répond pas exactement à la question : il exige un anneau axe vert plutôt que vert ou non évalué, et accepte un résultat Core Web Vitals orange. -#}
			{%- set offBand = [] -%}
			{%- for ring in rings -%}
			{%- if ring[0] == "average" or ring[0] == "poor" -%}
			{%- set offBand = (offBand.push(ring[0]), offBand) -%}
			{%- endif -%}
			{%- endfor -%}
			{#- « Hébergé soi-même » indique l’absence d’hébergeur plutôt qu’un hébergeur en particulier : c’est la catégorie dans laquelle tombe un nom de serveur seul. La carte n’affiche donc aucun nom. -#}
			{%- set hostName = entry.host.name if (entry.host and entry.host.id != "self-hosted") else null -%}
			{%- set generator = entry.generator or entry.presumedGenerator -%}
			{%- set noJs = entry.ownScreenshot.difference if entry.ownScreenshot else null -%}
			{#- Les trois dernières mesures, chacune représentée par les initiales de ses six bandes — « bon », « moyen », « mauvais » et « aucun » ne se distinguent pas tous par leur première lettre ; il s’agit donc d’un format de données, pas d’une nouvelle interprétation des bandes. L’historique étant enregistré du plus ancien au plus récent, les valeurs sont présentées dans cet ordre. -#}
			{%- set runs = [] -%}
			{%- set runCount = entry.history | length -%}
			{%- for run in entry.history -%}
			{%- if loop.index0 >= runCount - 3 -%}
			{%- set letters = [] -%}
			{%- for band in run.bands -%}{%- set letters = (letters.push(band[0]), letters) -%}{%- endfor -%}
			{%- set runs = (runs.push(letters | join("")), runs) -%}
			{%- endif -%}
			{%- endfor -%}
		,{{ [
			entry.slug,
			entry.displayUrl,
			entry.url,
			entry.groupName,
			entry.ranks.overall if (entry.ranks.overall and not offBand.length) else null,
			rings,
			(lab.weight.total | bytes) if lab else null,
			(lab.weight.requests | num) if lab else null,
			(lab.timings.lcp | ms) if lab else null,
			noJs,
			entry.clientRendered or false,
			(entry.latest.date | date("ymd")) if entry.latest else null,
			generator.name or null,
			hostName,
			(generator.presumed or false) if generator else false,
			runs
		] | dump | replace("</", "<\\/") | safe }}
			{%- endfor -%}
		]
	</script>

<script type="module">
/* Field order in each record above. */
/* SITE_URL, not URL: these are module-scope bindings, and `URL` would shadow
   the global constructor that builds the screenshot link below. */
const SLUG = 0, NAME = 1, SITE_URL = 2, GROUP = 3, RANK = 4, RINGS = 5,
	WEIGHT = 6, REQUESTS = 7, LCP = 8, NOJS = 9, EMPTY = 10, DATE = 11,
	GENERATOR = 12, HOST = 13, PRESUMED = 14, RUNS = 15;

/* Decodes the run bands above, which travel as initials to keep 1,500 records
   down to a page rather than a download. */
const BANDS = { g: "good", a: "average", p: "poor", n: "none" };

const SITES = JSON.parse(document.getElementById("og-sites").textContent).slice(1);
const BY_SLUG = new Map(SITES.map(site => [site[SLUG], site]));

/* The corpus grouped for the two selects. A site carries one category here —
   its primary — so a site belongs to exactly one list and the category can be
   derived from the site rather than tracked beside it. */
const BY_CATEGORY = new Map();

for (let site of SITES) {
	let label = site[GROUP] || "Uncategorized";

	if (!BY_CATEGORY.has(label)) {
		BY_CATEGORY.set(label, []);
	}

	BY_CATEGORY.get(label).push(site);
}

for (let sites of BY_CATEGORY.values()) {
	sites.sort((a, b) => a[NAME].localeCompare(b[NAME]));
}

/* The site's own order, with anything the report does not name — a category
   with no sites left, or a site filed under none — kept at the end rather than
   dropped. */
const CATEGORY_LIST = JSON.parse(document.getElementById("og-categories").textContent).slice(1);
const CATEGORY_ORDER = CATEGORY_LIST.map(([name]) => name);
const CATEGORY_IDS = new Map(CATEGORY_LIST);
const CATEGORIES = CATEGORY_ORDER.filter(label => BY_CATEGORY.has(label))
	.concat(Array.from(BY_CATEGORY.keys()).filter(label => !CATEGORY_ORDER.includes(label)));

const ORIGIN = "{{ meta.url }}";
const AVATAR_SERVICE = "{{ meta.avatarService }}";
const MEASURED_COUNT = {{ sites.stats.measured }};
const SCORE_LABELS = [{% for score in metrics.SCORES %}{{ score.label | dump | safe }}, {% endfor %}"Axe", "Core Web Vitals"];

/* The glyph for a verdict ring, matching axeRing and cwvRing: a tick passes, a
   cross fails badly, "!" is the middle case. The band decides it, and the band
   was decided by lib/rank.js at build time. */
const GLYPHS = { good: "✓", average: "!", poor: "✗" };

/* Anything thrown here leaves the card showing its placeholder values, which is
   indistinguishable from a real card at a glance. Report it where it will be
   seen. A window listener rather than a try/catch so it also catches a failure
   while this module is still being evaluated. */
window.addEventListener("error", event => showProblem(event.error || event.message));
window.addEventListener("unhandledrejection", event => showProblem(event.reason));

function showProblem(error) {
	let out = document.getElementById("ui-problem");

	if (out) {
		out.hidden = false;
		out.textContent = "This card did not render: " + ((error && error.stack) || error);
	}
}

const card = document.getElementById("og");
const eyebrow = document.getElementById("og-eyebrow");
const nameLine = document.getElementById("og-name");
const domain = document.getElementById("og-domain");
const favicon = document.getElementById("og-favicon");
const meta = document.getElementById("og-meta");
const ringRow = document.getElementById("og-rings");
const rings = ringRow.querySelectorAll(".ring");
const figures = document.getElementById("og-figures");
const unmeasured = document.getElementById("og-unmeasured");
const dateOut = document.getElementById("og-date");
const noJsFigure = document.getElementById("og-fig-nojs");
const runsFigure = document.getElementById("og-fig-runs");
const category = document.getElementById("field-category");
const siteCount = document.getElementById("ui-site-count");
const field = document.getElementById("field-site");
const screenshotOut = document.getElementById("ui-screenshot-url");
const openScreenshot = document.getElementById("open-screenshot");
const openReport = document.getElementById("open-report");
const openCategory = document.getElementById("open-category");

function figureValue(id) {
	return document.querySelector("#" + id + " .og-figure-value");
}

/* Only the band, the arc and the value change. The circumference is read back
   off the dash the shortcode already wrote, so the geometry lives in exactly
   one place — see `ring()` in buildawesome.config.js. */
function setRing(svg, band, text, pct, label) {
	svg.setAttribute("class", "ring ring-" + band);
	svg.setAttribute("aria-label", label);

	let arc = svg.querySelector(".ring-arc");
	let circumference = Number(arc.getAttribute("stroke-dasharray").split(" ")[1]);
	arc.setAttribute("stroke-dasharray", (circumference * (pct ?? 0)).toFixed(2) + " " + circumference);
	/* A null has no arc at all in the shortcode's output; hiding it is the same
	   picture, and keeps the element around for the next site. */
	arc.style.visibility = pct === null ? "hidden" : "";

	svg.querySelector(".ring-text").textContent = text;
}

function markFor(name, presumed) {
	if (!name) {
		return null;
	}

	let source = document.querySelector('#og-marks [data-mark="' + CSS.escape(name) + '"]');
	let mark = source && source.firstElementChild;

	if (!mark) {
		return null;
	}

	let clone = mark.cloneNode(true);

	/* A presumption is the category's claim rather than a measurement, faded
	   here the same way the shortcode fades it everywhere else. */
	if (presumed) {
		clone.classList.add("stack-presumed");
	}

	return clone;
}

function stackItem(name, presumed) {
	let item = document.createElement("span");
	item.className = "og-stack";
	let mark = markFor(name, presumed);

	if (mark) {
		item.append(mark);
	}

	item.append(name);
	return item;
}

/* No fitting is possible before the element is in the document, so this measures
   rather than guesses: shrink until the line stops overflowing its own box. */
function fitName() {
	let size = 76;
	nameLine.style.fontSize = size + "px";

	while (size > 32 && nameLine.scrollWidth > nameLine.clientWidth) {
		size -= 2;
		nameLine.style.fontSize = size + "px";
	}
}

function render(site) {
	ringRow.hidden = false;
	eyebrow.textContent = site[GROUP] || "";
	domain.textContent = site[NAME];

	if (AVATAR_SERVICE) {
		favicon.src = AVATAR_SERVICE.replace("{url}", encodeURIComponent(site[SITE_URL]));
	}

	meta.replaceChildren();

	if (site[RANK]) {
		let rank = document.createElement("span");
		rank.className = "og-rank";
		rank.textContent = "#" + site[RANK].toLocaleString("en-US");
		meta.append(rank, "of " + MEASURED_COUNT.toLocaleString("en-US") + " measured sites");
	}

	if (site[GENERATOR]) {
		meta.append(stackItem(site[GENERATOR], site[PRESUMED]));
	}

	if (site[HOST]) {
		meta.append(stackItem(site[HOST], false));
	}

	rings.forEach((svg, index) => {
		let [band, value] = site[RINGS][index];
		let isScore = index < rings.length - 2;
		let text = isScore ? (value ?? "–") : (GLYPHS[band] ?? "–");
		let pct = band === "none" ? null : (isScore ? value / 100 : 1);
		setRing(svg, band, text, pct, SCORE_LABELS[index] + ": " + text);
	});

	let measured = Boolean(site[DATE]);
	figures.hidden = !measured;
	unmeasured.hidden = measured;
	dateOut.textContent = measured ? site[DATE] : "";

	if (measured) {
		figureValue("og-fig-weight").textContent = site[WEIGHT];
		figureValue("og-fig-requests").textContent = site[REQUESTS];
		figureValue("og-fig-lcp").textContent = site[LCP];

		noJsFigure.hidden = site[NOJS] === null;

		if (site[NOJS] !== null) {
			let value = figureValue("og-fig-nojs");
			value.replaceChildren(site[NOJS] + "%");

			/* The page drew nothing without its scripts, which the percentage on
			   its own understates. */
			if (site[EMPTY]) {
				let flag = document.createElement("span");
				flag.className = "og-empty";
				let warning = document.querySelector('#og-marks [data-icon="warning"] > *');

				if (warning) {
					flag.append(warning.cloneNode(true));
				}

				flag.append("Empty");
				value.append(flag);
			}
		}
	}

	renderRuns(site[RUNS]);
	fitName();
}

/* The card with nothing in it: the wordmark and the rule it hangs on, and empty
   space where a site's figures would be. */
function renderBlank() {
	eyebrow.textContent = "";
	domain.textContent = "";
	favicon.removeAttribute("src");
	meta.replaceChildren();

	/* Six empty circles rather than no circles: the card keeps its shape, and
	   the gray band is the one that already means "nothing measured". */
	ringRow.hidden = false;
	rings.forEach((svg, index) => setRing(svg, "none", "", null, SCORE_LABELS[index]));

	figures.hidden = true;
	unmeasured.hidden = true;
	runsFigure.hidden = true;
	dateOut.textContent = "";
}

/* One row of six dots per run, newest on top. The records carry them oldest
   first, which is how history is stored; the reversal is a presentation choice
   and belongs here rather than in the data. */
function renderRuns(runs) {
	runsFigure.hidden = !runs.length;

	if (!runs.length) {
		return;
	}

	runsFigure.querySelector(".og-figure-label").textContent =
		runs.length === 1 ? "Last run" : "Last " + runs.length + " runs";

	runsFigure.querySelector(".og-runs").replaceChildren(...[...runs].reverse().map(run => {
		let row = document.createElement("span");
		row.className = "recents-dots";

		for (let letter of run) {
			let dot = document.createElement("span");
			dot.className = "recents-dot recents-dot-" + (BANDS[letter] ?? "none");
			row.append(dot);
		}

		return row;
	}));
}

function buildCategoryOptions() {
	/* The blank card, and the state the page opens in. A generator whose default
	   is somebody's site puts that site on every link anyone shares before they
	   have picked anything. */
	category.append(new Option("Select a category\u2026", ""));

	for (let label of CATEGORIES) {
		category.append(new Option(label, label));
	}
}

/* Refills the site select for one category. Replacing the options resets the
   select to its first one, which is what a category change should land on. */
function buildSiteOptions(label) {
	let sites = BY_CATEGORY.get(label) || [];

	field.replaceChildren(...sites.map(site => new Option(site[NAME], site[SLUG])));
	siteCount.textContent = sites.length
		? sites.length.toLocaleString("en-US") + (sites.length === 1 ? " site" : " sites")
		: "";
}

/* The image URL for one card. Built against the deployed origin rather than
   location: the screenshot service fetches a public URL, so a localhost one
   would not resolve. */
function showScreenshotUrl(query) {
	let screenshotUrl = "https://v1.screenshot.11ty.dev/" +
		encodeURIComponent(new URL("/opengraph/" + query, ORIGIN).toString()) + "/opengraph/";

	screenshotOut.textContent = screenshotUrl;
	openScreenshot.href = screenshotUrl;
}

function update() {
	let site = BY_SLUG.get(field.value);

	/* Before rendering, not after. These two are independent — the address bar
	   should name the selected site whether or not drawing its card works — and
	   with the order the other way round anything thrown while rendering leaves
	   the URL pointing at the previous site. */
	if (!site) {
		/* No site, no parameter: the bare URL is the blank card, and it has to
		   stay shareable as that rather than acquiring a site on arrival. */
		history.replaceState(null, "", location.pathname);
		showScreenshotUrl("");
		openReport.hidden = true;
		openCategory.hidden = true;
		document.title = "Open Graph card generator";
		renderBlank();
		return;
	}

	history.replaceState(null, "", "?site=" + encodeURIComponent(site[SLUG]));
	showScreenshotUrl("?site=" + encodeURIComponent(site[SLUG]));

	openReport.hidden = false;
	openReport.href = "/site/" + site[SLUG] + "/";
	openReport.textContent = "Full report for " + site[NAME];

	/* Hidden rather than dead where the category has no page of its own — a site
	   filed under none is the only case, and a link to /group// is worse than no
	   link at all. */
	let categoryId = CATEGORY_IDS.get(site[GROUP]);

	openCategory.hidden = !categoryId;
	openCategory.href = categoryId ? "/group/" + categoryId + "/" : "";
	openCategory.textContent = "Category: " + site[GROUP];
	document.title = site[NAME] + " · Open Graph card";

	render(site);
}

/* Both selects follow the URL, so a slug typed into the address bar or reached
   with the back button lands on that site rather than leaving them disagreeing.
   The category is derived from the site — it is not in the URL, and having it
   there would let the two contradict each other. */
function selectFromUrl() {
	let requested = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get("site");
	let site = BY_SLUG.get(requested);

	/* No parameter, or one naming nothing: the blank card rather than a guess. */
	category.value = site ? site[GROUP] || "Uncategorized" : "";
	buildSiteOptions(category.value);

	if (site) {
		field.value = site[SLUG];
	}
}

buildCategoryOptions();

/* Seeded from the query string, checked against the build-time list. */
selectFromUrl();

/* A new category means a new list, and the first site in it is the one the
   select is now showing — so the card and the URL follow it. */
category.addEventListener("change", () => {
	buildSiteOptions(category.value);
	update();
});

field.addEventListener("change", update);
window.addEventListener("popstate", () => {
	selectFromUrl();
	update();
});

document.getElementById("copy-link").addEventListener("click", async function () {
	await navigator.clipboard.writeText(location.href);
	this.textContent = "Copied!";
	setTimeout(() => (this.textContent = "Copy link to this card"), 1500);
});

update();

/* Fonts change the metrics, so measure the name again once they have loaded. */
await document.fonts.ready;
fitName();

/* A screenshot service can wait on this rather than capturing mid-fit. */
document.documentElement.classList.add("og-ready");
</script>

{% getBundle "fontawesome" %}

</body>
</html>
